{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805948-bloodline-iltani-discipline-m\u00e9rges","id":805948,"title":"Bloodline Iltani & Discipline M\u00e9rges","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-11T03:28:48-08:00","id":805948,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Bloodline Iltani & Discipline M\u00e9rges","content":"Hi everyone, second bloodline related thing i've posted here. I took it upon myself to try and update the Iltani from ancient mysteries and try change there from of blood sorcery to a discipline.<br /> As i saw it, their form of blood sorcery only really offered venom related powers and a modified version of riding the wave so I converted all the venom related things into a discipline.<br /> Hope you enjoy and feedback is welcomed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Iltani &amp; M\u00e9rges</span></u><br /> <br /> Bloodline</b>: Iltani<br /> <b>Clan</b>: Mekhet<br /> <b>Disciplines</b>: Auspex, Celerity, Obfuscate, <i><u><b>M\u00e9rges </b></u></i><br /> <b>Banes</b>: Mekhet Clan Bane + <u><b>Bloodline Bane - Seeping Beast</b></u><br /> Whenever the Iltani fails a discipline related roll they must make a Frenzy check, if they fail they fall into anger frenzy and assault the nearest target.<br /> If the Iltani dramatically fails, they anger frenzy on themselves.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u><b>Discipline: M\u00e9rges </b></u></span><br /> <br /> <u><b>Venomous Bite \u2022 </b></u><br /> <b>Dice pool</b>: Stamina + Occult + M\u00e9rges<br /> <b>Action</b>: Reflexive + instant (can only bite in a grapple)<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 0<br /> The Iltani concentrates her beast into a potent venom which can then be used to envenomate her victim with a bite. The bite does toxicity levels of damage equal to dots in M\u00e9rges and last hours equal to her blood potency. The Iltani can store doses of venom equal to her dots in M\u00e9rges a night.<br /> <br /> Damage modifier<br /> M\u00e9rges Level Dmg<br /> 1 Bashing (Mortals and Supernaturals)<br /> 2 Lethal (Lethal to Mortals. Bashing to Supernaturals)<br /> 3 Lethal (Lethal to Mortals and Supernaturals)<br /> 4 &quot; &quot;<br /> 5 &quot; &quot;<br /> <br /> The Iltani cannot draw vitae in the same turn as envenomating<br /> <br /> <u><b>Plant Venom \u2022\u2022 </b></u><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1 vitae<br /> <b>Dice pool</b>: none<br /> <b>Action:</b> instant<br /> The iltani can now coat surfaces in his venom.<br /> This can be over his fists or weapons. It cannot be placed on bullets can be put inside bullets.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Antidote \u2022\u2022\u2022 </b></u><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 2 vitae<br /> <b>Dice pool</b>: stamina + medicine + M\u00e9rges<br /> <b>Action</b>: instant.<br /> The Iltani has learnt how to create antidotes for his venom.<br /> This antidote must be administers via bite. Once administered all venom in a persons system is nullified.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Venom Mastery \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 </b></u><br /> At this level of M\u00e9rges the kindred has learnt to warp his venom into different types of venom.<br /> The M\u00e9rges picks 2 types of venom from the following list<br /> <br /> <b>- Lethal Venom</b> - lethal poison adds 2 levels of damage to their venom.<br /> <br /> <b>- Atrophising Venom</b> - hardens the muscles of the victims. The victim suffers a -3 to all physical actions.<br /> <br /> <b>- Anti-Coagulating Venom</b> - the venom bleeds vitae from the victim once per turn equal to half M\u00e9rges rounded up.<br /> <br /> <b>- Neurotoxin</b> - this venom affects the mind of the victim making it easier to get information out of the victim. Once administered the Iltani may ask one question to which he receives the answer for free. Every question asked after is resisted by stamina + resolve.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Living Toxin \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 </b></u><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 4 vitae<br /> <b>Dice pool</b>: stamina + occult + M\u00e9rges<br /> <b>Action</b>: instant<br /> <b>Duration</b>: scene<br /> The Iltani seeps venom from every pore on his body making him a walking toxin.<br /> Every physical attack he makes whilst Living Toxin is active instantly deals M\u00e9rges level in toxicity damage to his opponent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10405-lithiumdhalia","name":"LithiumDhalia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T07:33:07-08:00","id":806068,"title":"","content":"I'll add in the lore and physical descriptions of the bloodline eventually","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10405-lithiumdhalia","name":"LithiumDhalia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}